---
/* Nathan's signature, "Nathan Nixon" in a quick, confident hand: a big looped N, joined
   lowercase, the t and x crossed and the i dotted after, and a sweeping line under it all. It is
   a design mark for this site, drawn for it as single SVG strokes (Nathan asked for a made-up
   one, 2026-11-16). It is not his legal signature and is not a scan of one.

   The drawing lives in one cached file, public/assets/signature.svg, so a page only carries this
   small span (the closing has one on every page). The page shows it as a CSS mask over the ink
   colour, so it takes the theme's tokens (src/styles/ephemera/signature.css). With no script,
   under reduced motion and on paper it is the finished drawing (signature.svg#still). With a
   script, src/scripts/signature.js keeps an off-screen signature blank until it comes into view,
   then swaps in the moving file, whose own CSS draws each stroke in pen order. Each placement
   asks for the file with its own `?at=` so each one writes from its own start.

   The drawing is decoration. The name is in the markup as visually hidden text ("Signed, Nathan
   Nixon" by default, from site.ownerName); pass `said={false}` where the name would muddle a
   link's name, and say it beside it instead.

   Size and ink come from the holder: --sig-w (width) and --sig-ink (a colour token, the studio
   blue by default). Place it with `class`. `after` holds the pen a moment once it is in view
   (ms), for a signature on something still arriving. */
import '../../styles/ephemera/signature.css';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

interface Props {
  /** The visually hidden words that stand for the drawing, or false when they are said elsewhere. */
  said?: string | false;
  /** Extra classes, for placing it. */
  class?: string;
  /** Wait this many milliseconds after it comes into view before the pen starts. */
  after?: number;
  /** A short word naming the placement, so each placement's drawing runs on its own clock. */
  at?: string;
}
const { said = `Signed, ${site.ownerName}`, class: extra, after, at = 'here' } = Astro.props;
---

<span
  class={['sig', extra].filter(Boolean).join(' ')}
  data-sig
  data-sig-src={`/assets/signature.svg?at=${at}`}
  data-sig-after={after}
>
  {said && <span class="vh">{said}</span>}
</span>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/signature.js';
</script>
